  "ingredients": [
    "1/4 cup chicken broth",
    "6 tablespoon peanut butter",
    "2 tablespoon soy sauce (or coconut aminos)",
    "1 tablespoon fresh orange juice",
    "1 tablespoon lemon juice",
    "1/2 teaspoon sesame oil",
    "1/4 teaspoon ground coriander",
    "1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper",
    "2 teaspoon chili paste (such as sambal oelek)",
    "25 ounce boneless, skinless chicken thighs",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Add all of the ingredients except the chicken, salt, and pepper to a tall container.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/1-Add-Sauce-Ingredients-into-Container.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use an immersion blender to blend the ingredients, ensuring that the sauce has a smooth consistency throughout. Set aside until needed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/2-Immersion-Blend-Sauce-until-Smooth.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cube the chicken thighs and season to taste. Don't use too much salt, as the peanut sauce already contains salt from the soy sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/3-Cube-Chicken-and-Season.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat a dry pan over high heat. Once hot, add the chicken and sauté for about a minute.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/4-Add-Chicken-to-Hot-Pan.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "There should be quite a lot of excess moisture coming out of the chicken — simply pat it dry with a paper towel.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/5-Drain-Excess-Moisture-from-Chicken.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue cooking the chicken (and removing any excess moisture) until well browned.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/6-Continue-Cooking-Chicken-until-Browned.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once browned and cooked through, remove the pan from the heat. Pour the peanut sauce over the chicken and mix well to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/7-Remove-from-Heat-and-Stir-in-Sauce.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/thai-style-low-carb-peanut-chicken/#wprm-recipe-50817-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
